			<div class="content" id="post-content-1228294">
									

<p>I like this, and I've upvoted. I really like the angle you've taken on the cockatrice; the calcification is pretty horrifying. And I'm a sucker for well-done myth-based SCPs. Plus there are plenty of little details in here that are great. Couple examples:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-1000 has been noted to use natural body openings (mouth and eyes, primarily) on occasion</p>
</blockquote>
<p>(dear <em>god</em>)</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Subjects have responded poorly to questioning during feeding, resulting in a lack of direct data about this progression.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>However&#8230;</p>
<p>This is simply not as memorable as I would like. The detail work here (and, of course, your previous work) tells me that this could be even better. Also, this is pretty long for the amount of horror we get out of it; it could stand to be both expanded upon (with more delightful creepy horror stuff) and cut down.</p>
<p>What's here already is enough for an upvote, but I also look forward to seeing where this goes.</p>

